    "available_at": "2026-10-07T18:17:41.588524+00:00",
    "body": "Volkswagen opened pre-orders for the ID. Polo GTI, the first electric hot hatch to bear the iconic GTI badge.\nVolkswagen launches ID. Polo GTI pre-orders\nTo celebrate the GTI’s 50th anniversary, Volkswagen is “starting a new chapter” with the first all-electric GTI model.\nVolkswagen opened pre-orders for the ID. Polo GTI on Wednesday, starting at 39,995 euros, or about $45,000.\nThe first all-electric model to wear the GTI badge, “brings the legendary GTI driving pleasure into the electric future,” VW said.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nLike the first Golf GTI from 1976, the ID. Polo GTI uses a front-wheel-drive powertrain. The front-mounted electric motor delivers 222 hp (166 kW) and 213 lb-ft (290 Nm) of instant torque, enabling it to accelerate from 0 to 62 mph (0 to 100 km/h) in 6.8 seconds.\nThe electric hot hatch looks and feels like “a quintessential GTI” with the typical honeycomb pattern, the red stripe up front, and standard 19″ alloy wheels.\nVolkswagen ID. Polo GTI electric hot hatch (Source: Volkswagen)\nIt may not be the fastest, but Volkswagen promises the ID. Polo is a proper hot hatch that’s fun to drive.\nA fun electric hot hatch\nVolkswagen developed a new “GTI” driving profile that unlocks the vehicle’s full potential. At the push of a button on the steering wheel, the electric drive, steering, and suspension will automatically adjust to maximize performance and response.\nAn electronically controlled front axle transverse differential lock precisely distributes power to the front wheels, making it easier to corner and maneuver.\nVolkswagen ID. Polo GTI interior (Source: Volkswagen)\nInside, the interior is blacked out with sporty red elements. The electric hot hatch features a new GTI sports steering wheel and premium sports seats.\nBased on VW’s new cabin design, the ID. Polo GTI features a 10.25″ Digital Cockpit and 12.9″ infotainment display.\nLike the standard model, the ID. Polo GTI has a new “Retro Display” that transforms the instrument display and infotainment screen to resemble that of the first-generation Golf. Even the music sounds like it’s from the ’80s, as if it were a cassette.\nThe ID. Polo GTI uses the same 52 kWh nickel-manganese-cobalt (NMC) battery as the standard model, which provides a WLTP driving range of up to 431 km (267 miles).\nWith DC fast charging up to 105 kW, the vehicle’s battery can charge from 10% to 80% in about 24 minutes.\nMeasuring 4,096 mm long, 1,816 mm wide, and 1,514 mm tall, with a 2,599 mm wheelbase, the ID. Polo GTI is about the size of the gas-powered VW Polo.\nVolkswagen ID. Polo GTI (Source: Volkswagen)\nThanks to its compact drive modules and flat battery design, the electric hot hatch has 19 mm more interior space than the gas-powered Polo GTI. With the rear seats folded, the load capacity increases to 1,240 liters, compared with the Gas Polo’s 1,125 liters.\nThe Volkswagen ID. Polo GTI is now available to pre-order, starting at 39,995 euros. The standard ID. Polo is priced from 24,995 euros.\nIn early 2027, Volkswagen will open pre-orders for the more powerful ID.3 GTI , the second EV to wear the badge, and VW’s first rear-wheel-drive (RWD) GTI.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on Twitter , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
